<!--
  The hand-written half: the front door, the app, and the four guides.

  scripts/build-blog.mjs appends /blog/ and every post to a copy of this file on
  the way into dist, so the deployed sitemap is this plus the posts and nothing
  here needs editing when one is published.

  Everything else is deliberately absent rather than forgotten. The prerendered
  routes under /app are one document with one description repeated, so they
  canonicalize onto /app/ instead of appearing here. /chip is noindex. /apps is
  a 301. A sitemap listing near-duplicates asks to be judged on them, which is
  also the standard the guides have to meet: each one is here because it
  answers a different question, not because it is another page.

  The app is listed as /app/, with the slash, and build-blog.mjs adds /blog/
  and each post the same way. Each is a directory, and Netlify answers the bare
  form of a directory with a 301 to the slashed one, so the bare form is a
  redirect rather than a page and has no place in a sitemap.
-->
